A||||9||BAM-BAM||What  is the total out value of an 85GT?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||08-31-2000||08:25 PM|||| Well they finaly came, TODAY,(it's been 12 days since the accident) to look at my Fiero to assess the level of damage. I need some idea of what to expect if they decide to total my car. At what value do they say "Total It!" and if they do what is the fair replacement value of an 85GT? I would like to remain armed with the best info I can so they won't try to screw me. They already told me that my suspension mods won't be considered. So they come off this weekend and the old stuff goes back on. I should hear something tomorrow. Well, TIA for any info.<P> Later, BAM-BAM!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-31-2000||08:53 PM||||It really depends on how it was optioned, the mileage & overall condition.   '85 GT's can be had for as little as $500 or more than $5000.....it depends on a lot of factors.  <P>Overall, I would say that the '85 GT has a value of $2500.  That is what I generally see decent ones sell for.....add a few $$$ if yours was pristine and subtract a few $$$ if it had some issues.<P>Hopefully they give you a fair value for your GT.  If they total it will you buy it back?  I would be interested in it if you don't want it.  LMK.<P>Also,  I will be in Vegas Saturday night and all day Sunday before I head for L.A......I'd like to stop by to visit and see the carnage.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    LMK if that's possible.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||Oreif||09-01-2000||01:00 AM||||Kelly Blue Book Retail cost for a fully loaded 1985 GT is around $2700.00<BR>I think insurance companies go by retail for the "total" limit. But that doesn't leave much room for damage. If they go by wholesale your looking at $1500. This is why I have mine insured as a collector car and insured for it's appraised value. (Also because I get an EPA exemption   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  )<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-01-2000||02:14 AM||||Keep in mind that the adjusters like to get the paperwork done fast. They don't like having claims open.<P>Unless you *need* the money, just delay it and keep talking about "it's worth more". It's not like they can keep the money. <P>It's amazing how far many will go to get you to sign off the claim.<P>When my Ciera GT got clipped (2 base coat/6 clear coat and color sanded for a million years), they tried to get a cheap fix. I just waited, and waited and when they called I said it will cost more. Then I waited and waited and finally the guy said "whatever it costs is fine, I want to close this".  <P>Try it. The worst that happens is you get the same amount and burn some time.<P>My favortite comment was "We don't pay for color sanding". "Then make sure none of your customers hit my car, 'cause this time, you are....". And they did.<BR>TK<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||09-01-2000||07:52 AM||||  Thanks guys, I need all the info I can get. I have delt with claims adjusters once before, but it has been many years ago. I just want to get a fair shake. My luck has been terrible lately and I need a break.<P> Thanks, B-B<BR><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000005||Raydar||09-01-2000||11:40 AM||||Bam,<BR>Good luck. We recently went through an ordeal with my wife's Jeep. I hate insurance companies. And they say that organized crime is illegal...<P>Hey Orief,<BR>Is there any limit on the miles driven when you have it insured as a collector car?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-01-2000||12:47 PM||||Which wreck was this? I forget......<P>You want to get all your good stuff off before they write it up and cut a check. Once you take a check for a total it's their car.<P>You don't want to let them total it if you are going to repair it and keep it on the road. You'll get a salvage tittle when you buy it back. In allot of states that can cause a real pain in the rear.<P>If you are going to buy it back and part it then this doesn't matter. You can likely buy it back for $300-500.||||reg||1
Z||000007||cscougar||09-01-2000||02:39 PM||||My daughter recently had her 85 SE (73,000 mile, real clean vehicle) totalled.  The insurance company (not ours) gave us $2975.00 for the total value on it.  I was pleased since I had about $1500.00 in it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||cscougar||09-01-2000||02:41 PM||||I didn't tell you that I bought the car back on salvage for $75.00 so that made it a great deal. Put the interior in another 85 SE body for my son and I have the 3000 mile V-6 ready to go in my 85 GT.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BAM-BAM||09-02-2000||10:30 AM||||  Well, they told me yesterday that my car was a total loss even before they put it on the rack. Now, between you, and me, I believe it can be fixed. Worst case, a new right rear control arm, a couple new body panels, a new tire and wheel, a new sail panel, new windshield and it should be back to where it was. Most of these parts I can find in a wrecking yard. As for the total value, I'll have to wait untill next week to find out. My agent said to figure somewhere between the low and high book. Does this sound correct? If so, I'm looking around $3000.00 with the low being at $2275 and the high at $4205. I will buy it back and more than likely buy something else. Then I'll make the best of both and part the rest. I do want another 85GT though, it was the only year that the notchback GT was made. In my humble opinion, that makes it special. Now if I can find an 86GT for the right price, I may keep both and be half way to my eventual goal of owning a GT in every year. Of course with my luck I'll get $500.00 and still be without a vehical. Only time will tell. Peace, and thanks for the info. I love this place.<P> Later, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
